$\begin{aligned}
&  y=\tan ^{-1}(\sin \sqrt{x}) \\
& \Rightarrow \tan y=\sin \sqrt{x} \Rightarrow \sec ^2 y \cdot \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}} \cdot \frac{1}{2} \cos \sqrt{x} \\
& \Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{\cos \sqrt{x}}{2 \sqrt{x} \sec ^2 y}
\end{aligned}$
Tangent is parallel to $x$-axis
$\begin{aligned}
& \therefore \frac{d y}{d x} \Rightarrow \frac{\cos \sqrt{x}}{2 \sqrt{x} \sec ^2 y}=0 \\
& \Rightarrow \cos \sqrt{x}=0 \Rightarrow \cos \sqrt{x}=\cos \frac{\pi}{2} \\
& \Rightarrow x=\frac{\pi^2}{4} \Rightarrow \sqrt{x}= \pm \frac{\pi}{2} \Rightarrow \sin \sqrt{x}= \pm 1 \\
& \therefore y=\tan ^{-1}(\sin \sqrt{x})= \pm \frac{\pi}{4}
\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned} & \text {Let } f(x)=x^4 y^4 \\ & \text { And } a^2 x^4+b^2 y^4=c^6 \\ & \Rightarrow y^4=\frac{1}{b^2}\left(c^6-a^2 x^4\right) \\ & \therefore \quad f(x)=\mathrm{x}^4 \cdot \frac{1}{b^2}\left(c^6-a^2 x^4\right) \\ & =\frac{1}{b^2} x^4\left(c^6-a^2 x^4\right) \\ & f^{\prime}(x)=\frac{1}{b^2}\left(4 x^{3 c^6}-8 a^2 x^7\right) \\ & \end{aligned}$
for extrem point:
$\begin{aligned}
& f^{\prime}(\mathrm{x})=0 \Rightarrow 4 x^3\left(c^6-2 a^2 x^4\right)=0 \\
& \Rightarrow x=0 \text { or } x^4=\frac{c^6}{2 a^2}
\end{aligned}$
For maxima : $x=\frac{c^6}{2 a^2}\therefore$ The maximum value is :
$\begin{aligned}
& f\left(x=\left(\frac{c^6}{2 a^2}\right)^{\frac{1}{4}}\right) \\
& =\frac{c^6}{2 a^2} \cdot \frac{1}{b^2}\left[c^6-a^2 \cdot \frac{c^6}{2 a^2}\right] \\
& =\frac{c^6}{2 a^2 b^2} \cdot \frac{c^6}{2}=\frac{c^{12}}{4 a^2 b^2}
\end{aligned}$

